<p>
  <.link navigate="/hr/time">People → Time</.link>
  is where everyone logs the hours they work. It needs an employee record linked to your user
  (an admin sets that up on the employee's page).
</p>

<h2>Logging time</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Click <strong>Log time</strong>.</li>
  <li>Pick the date and the hours (quarter hours are fine, e.g. 1.25).</li>
  <li>
    Choose the <strong>pay type</strong>: regular, overtime, weekend, holiday, sick, vacation
    or unpaid.
  </li>
  <li>
    Optionally pick the <strong>customer</strong>
    and the <strong>project</strong>
    (a deal) you worked on, and say what you did.
  </li>
  <li>
    Tick <strong>Billable</strong> and enter an hourly rate when the customer should pay for it.
  </li>
</ol>
<p>
  The page shows one week at a time with a total per day. Use the arrows to move between weeks.
  You can edit or delete your own entries until they're billed. Admins see everyone's time,
  filter by employee and log time for others.
</p>

<h2>Reports</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Unbilled time</strong>
    — billable hours not invoiced yet, by customer, with their value.
  </li>
  <li><strong>Time activities by customer</strong> and <strong>by employee</strong>.</li>
  <li>
    <strong>Timesheet detail by employee</strong> — hours per day, regular, overtime and leave.
  </li>
  <li><strong>Time summary by pay type</strong> — hours per employee for each pay type.</li>
  <li><strong>Recent/edited time activities</strong> — what was logged or changed lately.</li>
</ul>
